A||N||3||trigger||Need all info about 3.4 push rod swaps!!||||1||
Z||000000||trigger||12-13-2001||06:29 PM||||I checked the archives and couldn't find anything.  What all is involved?  Will it bolt right up to the getrag?  Can I use 2.8 wiring and computer?  I'm helping put this in my friend's 87 2.5/5spd.  Thanks for any information you have.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||12-13-2001||08:28 PM||||3.4 pushrod from a 92-95 Camaro or Firebird will bolt right up to the tranny. You will have to drill holes on the other side of the block for the starter (drill template available). You will use Fiero 2.8 heads, intake, wiring and computer. The 5-spd in a 4-cyl is usually an Isuzu, not Getrag.||||reg||1
Z||000002||trigger||12-14-2001||01:17 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I know his has an izusu, we're swapping in a getrag.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-14-2001||04:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>...You will use Fiero 2.8 heads...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Camaro 3.4 heads are identical to the Fiero. No need to swap them. The Fiero intake system bolts right to them.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
